  beta = 1e-4: su2 5.97434e-7, u1_plus 6.16003e-5, u1_minus 3.06306e-5, u1_log_ratio 3.09697e-5

(c) P = I_1^2 - I_0 I_2 = sum_k p_k (beta/2)^{2k+2}:
  p_0..p_5 = ['1/2', '1/3', '5/48', '7/360', '7/2880', '11/50400'];  all p_k > 0 for k <= 60: True
  p_k = (2k+2)!/(k!(k+2)!((k+1)!)^2(k+2)) for all k <= 60: True  (so I_1^2 - I_0 I_2 >= (beta/2)^2/2 for all beta > 0, by the product formula)
  on (0, 4.03e-4], authors' route: P >= (beta/2)^2 (1/2 - 1.353e-8 - 7.71e-378) = (beta/2)^2 * 0.499999986465916 = (beta/2)^2 (1/2)(1 - 2.707e-8);  >= (1/2)(1 - 3e-8): True
  (since p_0 > 0 and p_k > 0 for the computed k, P >= (beta/2)^2/2 on (0, inf) would follow from positivity of all p_k, which I only checked to k = 60)

(d) the chain log(U_-/U_+) >= (U_- - U_+)/U_- >= 2 e^{-3 beta} P >= e^{-3beta}(1 - 1e-7) beta^2/4, at 2000 points of (0, 4.03e-4] (Numerical):
  all hold: True;  min over the grid of log(U_-/U_+)/(beta^2/4) = 0.999999986466

